ainly  room for future improvements in the  predictive ability to get more  predictions out of that intermediate  category into the high and low but  overall these are very promising results  and omniseek believes that their immune  report card assay can become a standard  for predicting response they're also  working on expanded versions of this  model that factor in  TCR beta repertoire results as well  you  so in summary I've shown you four of the  different solutions that we provide for  the study of immune oncology our TCR  beta long Reed and short Reed assays our  immune response expression Si and our  tumor mutation load assay and have given  some examples of how these can be  combined together to to provide the  basis of multi-dimensional biomarkers so  these are these are some more details  but I've run through these on the  individual assays and then just to  remind you these are all available in  the context of our ion chef and jean  studio s5 systems which have a high  degree of automation which makes them  extremely reproducible the gene studio  s5 itself is designed for scalability  and flexibility so we have multiple  different chips that can be used with a  sequencer to tailor to the level of  sequencing throughput that's necessary  for however many samples and need to be  analyzed and what the read requirements  are on that particular day and the  sequencing one of the strengths of the  sequencer is its speed the sequencing  and the analysis all happen extremely  fast the sequencing itself takes on the  order of two and a half or less hours  and these are provided in the context of  full sample to answer solutions we have  pre-configured and optimized by  informatics to get you all the way from  Apple through to answer and then lastly  I just like to give an advance notice  that we will have some follow-up  presentations to this one where my  colleague dr. Tim Looney will give two  more talks that are going to go into  more detail on some of the ass